  "full_text": "With everything in the open, it's not clear the Catholic Church couldn't really operate the same, right? Because they have to make bets on who's gonna be saved and who's not so that they can minimize. It's like selling insurance, you know what I mean? If you have rules that it's gonna operate going forward, then it's like actuaries and stuff. So the Catholic Church is kind of like gone. It can't operate in the light in the same way. So it's kind of over if you reveal all the secrets. So that is what it is. The Revelation said a thousand years of Christ's rule or something. But I don't know, the return of the king and stuff? I don't know. God himself ruling? I don't know.",
